---
import CalculatorLayout from '../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
import NypGpaCalculatorWidget from '../components/calculators/NypGpaCalculator';

const relatedCalculators = [
  { title: "RP GPA Calculator", path: "/rp-gpa-calculator" },
  { title: "SIT GPA Calculator", path: "/sit-gpa-calculator" },
  { title: "NUS GPA Calculator", path: "/nus-gpa-calculator" },
];
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="NYP GPA Calculator"
  description="Calculate your Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) for Nanyang Polytechnic (NYP). Manage your modules and check your eligibility for Diploma with Merit."
  category="Academic & Education"
  categoryPath="/categories/academic"
>
  <NypGpaCalculatorWidget client:load slot="calculator" />

  <Fragment slot="content">
    <h2>How to use the NYP GPA Calculator</h2>
    <p>
      The <strong>NYP GPA Calculator</strong> is built for students at Nanyang Polytechnic. NYP evaluates academic performance on a 4.0 grading scale. This tool helps you quickly figure out your semester GPA and your overall Cumulative GPA.
    </p>
    <p>
      To use the calculator:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>(Optional) Current Standing:</strong> If you have completed previous semesters, enter your current Cumulative GPA and the total number of graded credits.</li>
      <li><strong>Add Modules:</strong> Enter the name, credit units, and your expected grade for each module you are taking this semester.</li>
      <li><strong>Pass/Fail Modules:</strong> Select 'Pass' or 'Fail' for ungraded modules. These do not impact your GPA.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The calculator updates dynamically to show your projected grades and whether you are on track for a Diploma with Merit.
    </p>

    <h3>NYP Grade Points Table</h3>
    <p>Nanyang Polytechnic uses the following grade point system:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Distinction (DIST):</strong> 4.0 (Awarded to top performers)</li>
      <li><strong>A:</strong> 4.0 (Excellent)</li>
      <li><strong>B+:</strong> 3.5 (Very Good)</li>
      <li><strong>B:</strong> 3.0 (Good)</li>
      <li><strong>C+:</strong> 2.5 (Satisfactory)</li>
      <li><strong>C:</strong> 2.0 (Acceptable)</li>
      <li><strong>D+:</strong> 1.5 (Conditional Pass)</li>
      <li><strong>D:</strong> 1.0 (Conditional Pass)</li>
      <li><strong>F:</strong> 0.0 (Fail)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Diploma with Merit</h3>
    <p>
      Graduating with a Diploma with Merit at NYP generally requires you to be in the top 10% of your graduating cohort for your specific diploma. While the exact GPA cutoff varies, maintaining a CGPA of 3.5 and above makes you highly competitive.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="faq">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <details class="group bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 p-4 rounded-lg">
        <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          What is a Distinction grade?
          <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg fill="none" height="24" shape-rendering="geometricPrecision" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
          A Distinction (DIST) is occasionally awarded to the top few students in a module cohort. For the purpose of GPA calculation, it carries the same weight as an 'A' grade (4.0).
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="group bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 p-4 rounded-lg">
        <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          What happens if I fail a core module?
          <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg fill="none" height="24" shape-rendering="geometricPrecision" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
          An 'F' grade pulls your GPA down significantly as it awards 0.0 grade points while the credits are still counted. You will likely have to retake the core module in a subsequent semester to graduate.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="related">
    {relatedCalculators.map(calc => (
      <li>
        <a href={calc.path} class="group flex items-center p-2 rounded-md hover:bg-white dark:hover:bg-slate-700 transition-colors">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-2 text-slate-400 group-hover:text-teal-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 group-hover:text-teal-600 dark:group-hover:text-teal-400">{calc.title}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>
